# A real `application/cbor-seq` body: `GET /seq_notes/$subscribe` with
# `Accept: application/cbor-seq` against the Postgres-backed REST server
# (`cratestack-pg/tests/subscription_cbor_seq_shapes.rs`), captured once, as
# hex. The RPC route answers the same frames. A `ready` frame, then one `next` whose `event_id`
# and `data.id` are 16-byte CBOR byte strings and whose `amount` is text:
#   event_id 3143e143-5515-49fa-8e22-9f24d82d0a03
#   data     {id: 01234567-89ab-cdef-0123-456789abcdef, amount: "12.50000000", body: "hello"}

